ience  cry he said that the intent is to have  the audience share all the fields with  the characters from the fun and  adventures aspect to the fright and  peril but he shared that he thinks that  the Wonder and emotion are the most  important moments and that he hopes to  bring the audience to tears so you might  want to stock up on tissues before going  to see this movie  Astrid wasn't in the books according to  some  critics the movies are lacking a bit in  the girl-power Department the original  book series doesn't even have a female  character named Astrid one critic said  that the female character for the movie  was created solely for the purpose of  the romantic subplot another critic said  that Astrid is pretty much there from  the beginning to be the reward for  hiccup hiccup even said at the beginning  that he wants to become successful so he  can get a girlfriend critics think  Astrid has been reduced to just a prize  to be won even if she is a cooler edgier  stronger prize than other female  characters there is a hidden message  about intolerance in the hidden world  Dean Dubois shared that there is a  hidden theme in the hidden world that  you'll notice if you pay attention he  said there is a new villain named  grimille and grizzly who believes all  dragons are vermin and should be  destroyed diblock called him a very  intolerant character he said that  knowing what we know about dragons  it makes grimille and grizzly seem  especially cruel and rigid the ugliness  of intolerance is brought to life by him  hiccups idealism and hope-filled  attitude is a stark contrast to that  hatred shown by the villain hiccup  believes that coexistence is possible  but not everyone sees it that way  dreamer expired a bunch of employees  there were many delays in the releasing  of this third How to Train Your Dragon  movie this is because a bunch of  DreamWorks Animation employees got fired  according to Variety magazine the job  cuts came after a string of  disappoin